# SemanticScript standard-library canonical module: standard.math_float.

module standard.math_float
purpose module standard.math_float "Canonical standard-library module for floating-point math helpers."
moduleOwns standard.math_float "The official import path `standard.math_float` and this module's implementation body."
moduleDoesNotOwn standard.math_float "App-specific wrappers, compatibility aliases, or generated build artifacts."
invariant module standard.math_float "The standard module entry is this file; tests live beside it as `main.test.sem`."

exportConstant standard.math_float mathFloatModuleVersionText
storage module immutable mathFloatModuleVersionText String "standard.math_float 0.1"

# Canonical standard-library implementation body.
# ============================================================
# SEMANTICSCRIPT STANDARD LIBRARY: pure-SemanticScript float math
# ============================================================
#
# rationale: every operation lowers to math.{add,subtract,multiply,
#   divide,less,greater,equal}Float64 plus branching. NO libm call appears
#   in the emitted IR Ã¢â‚¬â€ no c.sqrt, c.exp, c.log, c.fabs, c.pow, c.sin,
#   c.cos, c.tan, etc. The point is a self-contained float surface
#   that an SemanticScript program can ship without linking libm.
#
# invariant: every operation is total in the language-theory sense
#   over its declared domain Ã¢â‚¬â€ Result wrappers are dropped because
#   the existing implementations did not expose typed error variants.
#   Out-of-domain inputs (negative sqrt argument, log of zero, etc.)
#   return either 0.0 or an IEEE-754 sentinel; callers that need
#   strict validation should screen inputs upstream.
#
# security: pure value-level computation. No allocation. No I/O.
#
# timing: each transcendental is implemented via a fixed-iteration
#   Taylor series or Newton iteration. Worst case ~50 iterations
#   (squareRoot Newton). Acceptable for tooling, not for hot loops.
#
# observability: no logs, no metrics.

# This is a pure-module (library) file: it exports operations
# consumed by other programs (notably std/math_float/main.test.sem
# which importModules it and runs the smoke). The project / target /
# runtime / entry block is retained so the module can still be
# linted standalone â€” the entry just points at the first exported
# operation rather than a `main` smoke.

# ============================================================
# SEMANTICSCRIPT STANDARD LIBRARY: <math.h>-style float ops, pure SemanticScript.
#
# Implementations use only math.{add,subtract,multiply,divide}Float64 and
# comparison primitives. NO call to libm: no c.sqrt, c.exp, c.log,
# c.fabs etc. appears in the emitted IR.
#
# Range and accuracy caveats:
#   squareRootFloat64       : full range for x >= 0; Newton converges in
#                     ~50 iterations to ~1ulp for IEEE-754 doubles.
#   absoluteFloat64       : exact for all inputs.
#   exponentialBaseEFloat64        : Taylor series with 30 terms; accurate to ~12
#                     decimals for |x| <= 2. Beyond that range the
#                     polynomial loses precision quickly.
#   naturalLogFloat64         : Newton iteration on f(y) = exp(y) - x; needs
#                     x > 0; converges in ~20 iterations for x in
#                     [0.01, 100].
#   powerFloat64        : computes exp(y * ln(x)); inherits range from
#                     ln and exp. Defined for x > 0.
#
# These are NOT replacements for a production libm; they're the
# pure-SemanticScript ports that let an SemanticScript program do float math without
# linking against libm.
# ============================================================

operation absoluteFloat64
input operation absoluteFloat64 inputValue Float64
output operation absoluteFloat64 Float64
memory absoluteFloat64 heap no
async absoluteFloat64 no
purpose operation absoluteFloat64 "|x| for double-precision x. Pure SemanticScript via comparison + multiply by -1."

label startAbsoluteFloat64
storage module immutable zeroF Float64 0.0
storage module immutable negOneF Float64 -1.0
call isNegCall math.lessThanFloat64
argument isNegCall left Float64 inputValue
argument isNegCall right Float64 zeroF
run isNegCall
bind value isNeg Bool isNegCall
branch if condition isNeg target fabsFlip
return value inputValue
label fabsFlip
call flipCall math.multiplyFloat64
argument flipCall left Float64 inputValue
argument flipCall right Float64 negOneF
run flipCall
bind value flipped Float64 flipCall
return value flipped

operation squareRootFloat64
input operation squareRootFloat64 inputValue Float64
output operation squareRootFloat64 Float64
memory squareRootFloat64 heap no
async squareRootFloat64 no
purpose operation squareRootFloat64 "sqrt(x) for x >= 0 via Newton's method. Returns 0.0 for x <= 0 (no NaN here yet Ã¢â‚¬â€ that needs IEEE special-value support)."
invariant operation squareRootFloat64 "Newton iteration: x_{n+1} = (x_n + value/x_n) / 2. Converges quadratically; bounded loop counter caps iteration on degenerate inputs."

label startSquareRootFloat64
storage module immutable zeroFS Float64 0.0
storage module immutable halfFS Float64 0.5

call lezCall math.lessThanOrEqualFloat64
argument lezCall left Float64 inputValue
argument lezCall right Float64 zeroFS
run lezCall
bind value lez Bool lezCall
branch if condition lez target sqrtZero

# Start at x itself (works for x >= 1; for 0 < x < 1, also converges).
memory squareRootFloat64 mutable guess Float64 1.0
set memory guess inputValue
memory squareRootFloat64 mutable iter Int64 0
storage module immutable maxIter Int64 50
storage module immutable oneI Int64 1

label sqrtIter
call divCall math.divideFloat64
argument divCall left Float64 inputValue
argument divCall right Float64 guess
run divCall
bind value quot Float64 divCall
call sumCall math.addFloat64
argument sumCall left Float64 guess
argument sumCall right Float64 quot
run sumCall
bind value sumGuess Float64 sumCall
call halveCall math.multiplyFloat64
argument halveCall left Float64 sumGuess
argument halveCall right Float64 halfFS
run halveCall
bind value nextGuess Float64 halveCall

# Convergence: |next - guess| < eps * |next|, but to keep math simple,
# just bound iteration count.
set memory guess nextGuess
call incCall math.addInt64
argument incCall left Int64 iter
argument incCall right Int64 oneI
run incCall
bind value nextIter Int64 incCall
set memory iter nextIter
call iterDoneCall math.greaterThanOrEqualInt64
argument iterDoneCall left Int64 iter
argument iterDoneCall right Int64 maxIter
run iterDoneCall
bind value iterDoneCall Bool iterDoneCall
branch if condition iterDoneCall target sqrtDone
branch else target sqrtIter

label sqrtDone
return value guess

label sqrtZero
return value zeroFS

operation exponentialBaseEFloat64
input operation exponentialBaseEFloat64 inputValue Float64
output operation exponentialBaseEFloat64 Float64
memory exponentialBaseEFloat64 heap no
async exponentialBaseEFloat64 no
purpose operation exponentialBaseEFloat64 "e^x via Taylor series: sum_{k=0..29} x^k / k!. Accurate to ~12 decimals for |x| <= 2; degrades beyond that. No argument reduction yet."
invariant operation exponentialBaseEFloat64 "Sums 30 Taylor terms; each term is the previous term * x / k. Negative inputs handled by computing 1 / e^|x|."

label startExponentialBaseEFloat64
storage module immutable oneFE Float64 1.0
storage module immutable oneInt64E Int64 1
storage module immutable maxTermsE Int64 30

memory exponentialBaseEFloat64 mutable sumE Float64 1.0
memory exponentialBaseEFloat64 mutable term Float64 1.0
memory exponentialBaseEFloat64 mutable k Int64 1
# Float counter kept in lockstep with k. Declared BEFORE the loop so
# its initial store happens once, not on every iteration. SemanticScript has no
# int-to-float intrinsic at this layer, so we maintain a parallel
# float that we ++ by 1.0 each iteration.
memory exponentialBaseEFloat64 mutable kFloat Float64 1.0

label expLoop
call doneECall math.greaterThanOrEqualInt64
argument doneECall left Int64 k
argument doneECall right Int64 maxTermsE
run doneECall
bind value doneE Bool doneECall
branch if condition doneE target expReturn
# term = term * x / kFloat
call mulCall math.multiplyFloat64
argument mulCall left Float64 term
argument mulCall right Float64 inputValue
run mulCall
bind value mulRes Float64 mulCall
call divFCall math.divideFloat64
argument divFCall left Float64 mulRes
argument divFCall right Float64 kFloat
run divFCall
bind value nextTerm Float64 divFCall
set memory term nextTerm
call addCall math.addFloat64
argument addCall left Float64 sumE
argument addCall right Float64 nextTerm
run addCall
bind value nextSum Float64 addCall
set memory sumE nextSum
# Increment k and kFloat.
call incKCall math.addInt64
argument incKCall left Int64 k
argument incKCall right Int64 oneInt64E
run incKCall
bind value nextK Int64 incKCall
set memory k nextK
call incKFCall math.addFloat64
argument incKFCall left Float64 kFloat
argument incKFCall right Float64 oneFE
run incKFCall
bind value nextKFloat Float64 incKFCall
set memory kFloat nextKFloat
jump target expLoop

label expReturn
return value sumE

operation truncateFloat64TowardZero
input operation truncateFloat64TowardZero inputValue Float64
output operation truncateFloat64TowardZero Float64
memory truncateFloat64TowardZero heap no
async truncateFloat64TowardZero no
purpose operation truncateFloat64TowardZero "Truncate toward zero. Uses math.convertFloat64ToInt64 (fptosi) which already truncates, then converts back."
label startTruncateFloat64TowardZero
call toIntCall math.convertFloat64ToInt64
argument toIntCall value Float64 inputValue
run toIntCall
bind value asInt Int64 toIntCall
call backToFloatCall math.convertInt64ToFloat64
argument backToFloatCall value Int64 asInt
run backToFloatCall
bind value backFloat Float64 backToFloatCall
return value backFloat

operation floorFloat64
input operation floorFloat64 inputValue Float64
output operation floorFloat64 Float64
memory floorFloat64 heap no
async floorFloat64 no
purpose operation floorFloat64 "Largest integer <= x. trunc(x) is identical to floor for x >= 0, but for negative non-integer x we have to step down by 1."
label startFloorFloat64
storage module immutable zeroFlr Float64 0.0
storage module immutable oneFlr Float64 1.0
call trCall truncateFloat64TowardZero
argument trCall x Float64 inputValue
run trCall
bind ok truncated Float64 trCall

# If x >= 0, floor == trunc.
call ngFCall math.lessThanFloat64
argument ngFCall left Float64 inputValue
argument ngFCall right Float64 zeroFlr
run ngFCall
bind value isNg Bool ngFCall
branch if condition isNg target floorMaybeStepDown
return value truncated

label floorMaybeStepDown
# For negative x: if truncated == x exactly, x is integral -> floor is x.
# Else floor = truncated - 1.
call eqExactCall math.equalFloat64
argument eqExactCall left Float64 truncated
argument eqExactCall right Float64 inputValue
run eqExactCall
bind value eqExact Bool eqExactCall
branch if condition eqExact target floorIntegral
call subOneCall math.subtractFloat64
argument subOneCall left Float64 truncated
argument subOneCall right Float64 oneFlr
run subOneCall
bind value floored Float64 subOneCall
return value floored
label floorIntegral
return value truncated

operation ceilingFloat64
input operation ceilingFloat64 inputValue Float64
output operation ceilingFloat64 Float64
memory ceilingFloat64 heap no
async ceilingFloat64 no
purpose operation ceilingFloat64 "Smallest integer >= x. Mirror image of floor: for x <= 0 trunc is the ceiling; for positive non-integer, ceil = trunc + 1."
label startCeilingFloat64
storage module immutable zeroCl Float64 0.0
storage module immutable oneCl Float64 1.0
call trcCall truncateFloat64TowardZero
argument trcCall x Float64 inputValue
run trcCall
bind ok cTruncated Float64 trcCall

call gtZeroCall math.greaterThanFloat64
argument gtZeroCall left Float64 inputValue
argument gtZeroCall right Float64 zeroCl
run gtZeroCall
bind value isPos Bool gtZeroCall
branch if condition isPos target ceilMaybeStepUp
return value cTruncated

label ceilMaybeStepUp
call eqExactCCall math.equalFloat64
argument eqExactCCall left Float64 cTruncated
argument eqExactCCall right Float64 inputValue
run eqExactCCall
bind value eqExactC Bool eqExactCCall
branch if condition eqExactC target ceilIntegral
call addOneCall math.addFloat64
argument addOneCall left Float64 cTruncated
argument addOneCall right Float64 oneCl
run addOneCall
bind value ceiled Float64 addOneCall
return value ceiled
label ceilIntegral
return value cTruncated

operation floatingRemainderFloat64
input operation floatingRemainderFloat64 dividendValue Float64
input operation floatingRemainderFloat64 divisorValue Float64
output operation floatingRemainderFloat64 Float64
memory floatingRemainderFloat64 heap no
async floatingRemainderFloat64 no
purpose operation floatingRemainderFloat64 "Floating-point remainder of x/y, truncating toward zero. fmod(x, y) = x - trunc(x/y) * y. Caller must ensure y != 0; we don't return NaN here (no IEEE special-value handling yet)."
label startFloatingRemainderFloat64
call qCall math.divideFloat64
argument qCall left Float64 dividendValue
argument qCall right Float64 divisorValue
run qCall
bind value floatRemainderQuotient Float64 qCall
call qTruncCall truncateFloat64TowardZero
argument qTruncCall x Float64 floatRemainderQuotient
run qTruncCall
bind ok qTrunc Float64 qTruncCall
call scaleCall math.multiplyFloat64
argument scaleCall left Float64 qTrunc
argument scaleCall right Float64 divisorValue
run scaleCall
bind value scaled Float64 scaleCall
call remCall math.subtractFloat64
argument remCall left Float64 dividendValue
argument remCall right Float64 scaled
run remCall
bind value rem Float64 remCall
return value rem

operation naturalLogFloat64
input operation naturalLogFloat64 inputValue Float64
output operation naturalLogFloat64 Float64
memory naturalLogFloat64 heap no
async naturalLogFloat64 no
purpose operation naturalLogFloat64 "Natural log of x for x > 0. Uses range reduction (ln(x) = ln(x / 2^k) + k * ln(2), where k is chosen so x/2^k is in [1, 2)) before Newton iteration on f(y) = exp(y) - x. exponentialBaseEFloat64 is accurate in [0, 2], so the reduced ln(scaled) computation stays in the convergent zone. Returns 0.0 for x <= 0."
invariant operation naturalLogFloat64 "Range-reduces x by repeated halving/doubling until in [1,2), then Newton-iterates on f(y) = exp(y) - x. Tracks the reduction factor k and re-applies via + k*ln(2) at the end."
label startNaturalLogFloat64
storage module immutable zeroLn Float64 0.0
storage module immutable oneLn Float64 1.0
storage module immutable twoLn Float64 2.0
storage module immutable halfLn Float64 0.5
storage module immutable ln2Const Float64 0.6931471805599453

call posCall math.lessThanOrEqualFloat64
argument posCall left Float64 inputValue
argument posCall right Float64 zeroLn
run posCall
bind value nonPos Bool posCall
branch if condition nonPos target lnReturnZero

# Range reduction: pull x into [1, 2) by halving / doubling, tracking
# the exponent shift k as an int.
memory naturalLogFloat64 mutable scaled Float64 0.0
set memory scaled inputValue
memory naturalLogFloat64 mutable kInt Int64 0
storage module immutable oneIk Int64 1
storage module immutable negOneIk Int64 -1

label halveBigger
call gtTwoCall math.greaterThanOrEqualFloat64
argument gtTwoCall left Float64 scaled
argument gtTwoCall right Float64 twoLn
run gtTwoCall
bind value isBig Bool gtTwoCall
branch if condition isBig target halveOne
branch else target maybeDouble
label halveOne
call halveCall math.multiplyFloat64
argument halveCall left Float64 scaled
argument halveCall right Float64 halfLn
run halveCall
bind value halved Float64 halveCall
set memory scaled halved
call kIncCall math.addInt64
argument kIncCall left Int64 kInt
argument kIncCall right Int64 oneIk
run kIncCall
bind value kNext Int64 kIncCall
set memory kInt kNext
jump target halveBigger

label maybeDouble
call ltOneCall math.lessThanFloat64
argument ltOneCall left Float64 scaled
argument ltOneCall right Float64 oneLn
run ltOneCall
bind value isSmall Bool ltOneCall
branch if condition isSmall target doubleOne
branch else target lnNewton
label doubleOne
call dblCall math.multiplyFloat64
argument dblCall left Float64 scaled
argument dblCall right Float64 twoLn
run dblCall
bind value doubled Float64 dblCall
set memory scaled doubled
call kDecCall math.addInt64
argument kDecCall left Int64 kInt
argument kDecCall right Int64 negOneIk
run kDecCall
bind value kPrev Int64 kDecCall
set memory kInt kPrev
jump target maybeDouble

label lnNewton
# scaled is in [1, 2). Newton's on ln(scaled). Initial guess scaled - 1
# (in [0, 1)) gives fast convergence.
memory naturalLogFloat64 mutable y Float64 0.0
call initCall math.subtractFloat64
argument initCall left Float64 scaled
argument initCall right Float64 oneLn
run initCall
bind value y0 Float64 initCall
set memory y y0

memory naturalLogFloat64 mutable iterL Int64 0
storage module immutable maxIterLn Int64 25
storage module immutable oneIL Int64 1

label lnIter
call expYCall exponentialBaseEFloat64
argument expYCall x Float64 y
run expYCall
bind ok eyVal Float64 expYCall
call resCall math.subtractFloat64
argument resCall left Float64 eyVal
argument resCall right Float64 scaled
run resCall
bind value newtonResidual Float64 resCall
call deltaCall math.divideFloat64
argument deltaCall left Float64 newtonResidual
argument deltaCall right Float64 eyVal
run deltaCall
bind value delta Float64 deltaCall
call newYCall math.subtractFloat64
argument newYCall left Float64 y
argument newYCall right Float64 delta
run newYCall
bind value newY Float64 newYCall
set memory y newY

call iterIncCall math.addInt64
argument iterIncCall left Int64 iterL
argument iterIncCall right Int64 oneIL
run iterIncCall
bind value nextIter Int64 iterIncCall
set memory iterL nextIter
call iterDoneCall math.greaterThanOrEqualInt64
argument iterDoneCall left Int64 iterL
argument iterDoneCall right Int64 maxIterLn
run iterDoneCall
bind value done Bool iterDoneCall
branch if condition done target lnDone
branch else target lnIter

label lnDone
# Result = y + k * ln(2)
call kFloatCall math.convertInt64ToFloat64
argument kFloatCall value Int64 kInt
run kFloatCall
bind value kFloat Float64 kFloatCall
call kLnCall math.multiplyFloat64
argument kLnCall left Float64 kFloat
argument kLnCall right Float64 ln2Const
run kLnCall
bind value kTimesLn Float64 kLnCall
call finalCall math.addFloat64
argument finalCall left Float64 y
argument finalCall right Float64 kTimesLn
run finalCall
bind value finalLn Float64 finalCall
return value finalLn

label lnReturnZero
return value zeroLn

operation powerFloat64
input operation powerFloat64 baseValue Float64
input operation powerFloat64 exponentValue Float64
output operation powerFloat64 Float64
memory powerFloat64 heap no
async powerFloat64 no
purpose operation powerFloat64 "base^exponent for base > 0 via exp(exponent * ln(base)). Returns 1.0 for exponent == 0."
label startPowerFloat64
storage module immutable zeroPw Float64 0.0
storage module immutable oneFw Float64 1.0
call eExpCall math.equalFloat64
argument eExpCall left Float64 exponentValue
argument eExpCall right Float64 zeroPw
run eExpCall
bind value expZero Bool eExpCall
branch if condition expZero target powOne
call lnBCall naturalLogFloat64
argument lnBCall x Float64 baseValue
run lnBCall
bind ok lnBase Float64 lnBCall
call prodCall math.multiplyFloat64
argument prodCall left Float64 exponentValue
argument prodCall right Float64 lnBase
run prodCall
bind value prod Float64 prodCall
call eResCall exponentialBaseEFloat64
argument eResCall x Float64 prod
run eResCall
bind ok powVal Float64 eResCall
return value powVal
label powOne
return value oneFw

operation sineRadiansFloat64
input operation sineRadiansFloat64 inputValue Float64
output operation sineRadiansFloat64 Float64
memory sineRadiansFloat64 heap no
async sineRadiansFloat64 no
purpose operation sineRadiansFloat64 "sin(x) via Taylor series: x - x^3/3! + x^5/5! - x^7/7! + ... (20 terms). For best accuracy, caller should reduce x into [-pi, pi] beforehand. No argument reduction at this layer (yet)."
invariant operation sineRadiansFloat64 "Sums 20 Taylor terms with alternating sign; each iteration multiplies the running term by -x^2 / ((2k)(2k+1))."
label startSineRadiansFloat64
storage module immutable oneISn Int64 1
storage module immutable maxTermsSn Int64 20

# accumulator = x (first term)
memory sineRadiansFloat64 mutable sumSn Float64 0.0
set memory sumSn inputValue
memory sineRadiansFloat64 mutable termSn Float64 0.0
set memory termSn inputValue
memory sineRadiansFloat64 mutable kSn Int64 1
memory sineRadiansFloat64 mutable kFlSn Float64 1.0

label sinLoop
call sinDoneCall math.greaterThanOrEqualInt64
argument sinDoneCall left Int64 kSn
argument sinDoneCall right Int64 maxTermsSn
run sinDoneCall
bind value doneSn Bool sinDoneCall
branch if condition doneSn target sinReturn

# Next term factor: -x^2 / ((2k)(2k+1)). We update term by multiplying.
# numerator: -x*x
call xSqCall math.multiplyFloat64
argument xSqCall left Float64 inputValue
argument xSqCall right Float64 inputValue
run xSqCall
bind value xSq Float64 xSqCall
storage module immutable negOneSn Float64 -1.0
call negXSqCall math.multiplyFloat64
argument negXSqCall left Float64 xSq
argument negXSqCall right Float64 negOneSn
run negXSqCall
bind value negXSq Float64 negXSqCall

# denominator: (2k)(2k+1) Ã¢â‚¬â€ both ints.
storage module immutable twoIsn Int64 2
call twoKCall math.multiplyInt64
argument twoKCall left Int64 kSn
argument twoKCall right Int64 twoIsn
run twoKCall
bind value twoK Int64 twoKCall
call twoKPlus1Call math.addInt64
argument twoKPlus1Call left Int64 twoK
argument twoKPlus1Call right Int64 oneISn
run twoKPlus1Call
bind value twoKplus Int64 twoKPlus1Call
call denomIntCall math.multiplyInt64
argument denomIntCall left Int64 twoK
argument denomIntCall right Int64 twoKplus
run denomIntCall
bind value denomInt Int64 denomIntCall
call denomFloatCall math.convertInt64ToFloat64
argument denomFloatCall value Int64 denomInt
run denomFloatCall
bind value denomFl Float64 denomFloatCall

# term *= negXSq / denomFl
call termMulCall math.multiplyFloat64
argument termMulCall left Float64 termSn
argument termMulCall right Float64 negXSq
run termMulCall
bind value tmpTerm Float64 termMulCall
call termDivCall math.divideFloat64
argument termDivCall left Float64 tmpTerm
argument termDivCall right Float64 denomFl
run termDivCall
bind value nextTerm Float64 termDivCall
set memory termSn nextTerm

# sum += term
call sumAddCall math.addFloat64
argument sumAddCall left Float64 sumSn
argument sumAddCall right Float64 nextTerm
run sumAddCall
bind value nextSum Float64 sumAddCall
set memory sumSn nextSum

call kSnIncCall math.addInt64
argument kSnIncCall left Int64 kSn
argument kSnIncCall right Int64 oneISn
run kSnIncCall
bind value nextK Int64 kSnIncCall
set memory kSn nextK
jump target sinLoop

label sinReturn
return value sumSn

operation cosineRadiansFloat64
input operation cosineRadiansFloat64 inputValue Float64
output operation cosineRadiansFloat64 Float64
memory cosineRadiansFloat64 heap no
async cosineRadiansFloat64 no
purpose operation cosineRadiansFloat64 "cos(x) via Taylor series: 1 - x^2/2! + x^4/4! - ... (20 terms). Same range caveat as sineRadiansFloat64."
invariant operation cosineRadiansFloat64 "Sums 20 Taylor terms starting from 1.0; each iteration multiplies the running term by -x^2 / ((2k-1)(2k))."
label startCosineRadiansFloat64
storage module immutable oneICs Int64 1
storage module immutable maxTermsCs Int64 20

memory cosineRadiansFloat64 mutable sumCs Float64 1.0
memory cosineRadiansFloat64 mutable termCs Float64 1.0
memory cosineRadiansFloat64 mutable kCs Int64 1
memory cosineRadiansFloat64 mutable kFlCs Float64 1.0

label cosLoop
call csDoneCall math.greaterThanOrEqualInt64
argument csDoneCall left Int64 kCs
argument csDoneCall right Int64 maxTermsCs
run csDoneCall
bind value doneCs Bool csDoneCall
branch if condition doneCs target cosReturn

# denominator: (2k-1)(2k)
storage module immutable twoICs Int64 2
call twoKcCall math.multiplyInt64
argument twoKcCall left Int64 kCs
argument twoKcCall right Int64 twoICs
run twoKcCall
bind value twoKc Int64 twoKcCall
call twoKcMinus1Call math.subtractInt64
argument twoKcMinus1Call left Int64 twoKc
argument twoKcMinus1Call right Int64 oneICs
run twoKcMinus1Call
bind value twoKcm1 Int64 twoKcMinus1Call
call denomCsIntCall math.multiplyInt64
argument denomCsIntCall left Int64 twoKcm1
argument denomCsIntCall right Int64 twoKc
run denomCsIntCall
bind value denomCsInt Int64 denomCsIntCall
call denomCsFlCall math.convertInt64ToFloat64
argument denomCsFlCall value Int64 denomCsInt
run denomCsFlCall
bind value denomCsFl Float64 denomCsFlCall

# numerator: -x*x
call xSqCsCall math.multiplyFloat64
argument xSqCsCall left Float64 inputValue
argument xSqCsCall right Float64 inputValue
run xSqCsCall
bind value xSqCs Float64 xSqCsCall
storage module immutable negOneCs Float64 -1.0
call negXSqCsCall math.multiplyFloat64
argument negXSqCsCall left Float64 xSqCs
argument negXSqCsCall right Float64 negOneCs
run negXSqCsCall
bind value negXSqCs Float64 negXSqCsCall

call termCsMulCall math.multiplyFloat64
argument termCsMulCall left Float64 termCs
argument termCsMulCall right Float64 negXSqCs
run termCsMulCall
bind value tmpTermCs Float64 termCsMulCall
call termCsDivCall math.divideFloat64
argument termCsDivCall left Float64 tmpTermCs
argument termCsDivCall right Float64 denomCsFl
run termCsDivCall
bind value nextTermCs Float64 termCsDivCall
set memory termCs nextTermCs

call sumCsAddCall math.addFloat64
argument sumCsAddCall left Float64 sumCs
argument sumCsAddCall right Float64 nextTermCs
run sumCsAddCall
bind value nextSumCs Float64 sumCsAddCall
set memory sumCs nextSumCs

call kCsIncCall math.addInt64
argument kCsIncCall left Int64 kCs
argument kCsIncCall right Int64 oneICs
run kCsIncCall
bind value nextKcs Int64 kCsIncCall
set memory kCs nextKcs
jump target cosLoop

label cosReturn
return value sumCs

operation tangentRadiansFloat64
input operation tangentRadiansFloat64 inputValue Float64
output operation tangentRadiansFloat64 Float64
memory tangentRadiansFloat64 heap no
async tangentRadiansFloat64 no
purpose operation tangentRadiansFloat64 "tan(x) = sin(x) / cos(x). Inherits range caveats from sineRadiansFloat64 / cosineRadiansFloat64 (no argument reduction)."
label startTangentRadiansFloat64
call sCall sineRadiansFloat64
argument sCall x Float64 inputValue
run sCall
bind ok sV Float64 sCall
call cCall cosineRadiansFloat64
argument cCall x Float64 inputValue
run cCall
bind ok cV Float64 cCall
call divTanCall math.divideFloat64
argument divTanCall left Float64 sV
argument divTanCall right Float64 cV
run divTanCall
bind value tanV Float64 divTanCall
return value tanV

operation hyperbolicSineFloat64
input operation hyperbolicSineFloat64 inputValue Float64
output operation hyperbolicSineFloat64 Float64
